that Iksvāku, lord of the earth, 'What is this that you have gathered as the fruit of your encounter with me.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.627,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-19-16"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7019018","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cc450c5b58c88150059e6ee360058417cd41ae8bdadaf5d8c910a1b36b7e070c","compact":"8151e025d4345a7baab61028ee300f0f8e454a9e7ffbc4406121cb2626e67297","nasal":"8151e025d4345a7baab61028ee300f0f8e454a9e7ffbc4406121cb2626e67297"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-19-19","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":19,"verse":19,"english":"O king, there is none in this triune sphere that can combat with me. Having hitherto been sunk in lunacy, you have not heard of my strength.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.742,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-19-17"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7019019","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"0820e3c20804bbb2d5d7c8b0476b7093f45cfeef87740a3be4be8fad45b7d974","compact":"b1092a38b27693e958de4bcd0d02a9bf857f985c9216366119c9cd11fb876e2a","nasal":"f52c287c1d0cd15149dd5ac0b8195a4b8f0398e29501de7cd05597253326b933"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-19-20","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":19,"verse":20,"english":"As he was speaking thus, the king, whose sounds were fast running out said: 'What can I do in this matter. Verily time is incapable of being controlled.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.794,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-19-18"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7019020","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7f428df86a0ce40d88adb53acf0a85a6bf2b1f439ad5ce0503fd68d7583b04a0","compact":"f3dd6e0ce0406669f9ead03a90d80ef11097d379401f99d7b4bf1f18239e309c","nasal":"e6181cb85bf9d5c043019f707615843bee390b6e3ec9dc4a8e0f9fb36207f05d"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-19-21","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":19,"verse":21,"english":"I have been overcome by Time; you are merely an instrument. What can I do now, when I am going to-lose my life? I never turned away from fight; I have been slain fighting.","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.864,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-19-19"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7019021","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"7256bcfabc6a6aec4d6b56e879cb20116de69d79ad34adee251cb9c26f676b87","compact":"01a9e23d1d752041e54481468e8edd6995a2ce8de887145d80ab2f70b0b0e41b","nasal":"a68f5e98d7ba2766d47798115e58417267432ca81e081aa58f72b93f07c57090"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-19-22","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":19,"verse":22,"english":"I have been overcome by Time; you are merely an instrument. What can I do now, when I am going to-lose my life? I never turned away from fight; I have been slain fighting. But, O Raksasas, I shall tell you something in consequence of the disgrace that the Ikşvāku race has met with (today). If I have practised charity, if I have offered oblations into fire, if I have carried on pious penances, if i have governed my people well, then be my words verified!","alignment":{"type":"split","confidence":0.458,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-19-19","DUTT-7-19-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7019022","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"aeaaa4439410dca12fe1333485a03f3e88612615e079f24714e8ad5551b134f0","compact":"94843d6a052e5d59948296f235fe71c3834a4fdf4c4708c8b44a4a724f97650c","nasal":"94843d6a052e5d59948296f235fe71c3834a4fdf4c4708c8b44a4a724f97650c"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-19-23","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":19,"verse":23,"english":"But, O Raksasas, I shall tell you something in consequence of the disgrace that the Ikşvāku race has met with (today). If I have practised charity, if I have offered oblations into fire, if I have carried on pious penances, if i have governed my people well, then be my words verified!","alignment":{"type":"grouped","confidence":0.869,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-19-20"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7019023","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"4b3eb09d61629a1ef33697f71dbd16b5ba7766bc968e8a7891ddba8bd76c50e6","compact":"d2bdc537253d1f1cd5e9bceba08307746f1c63715e1c767ef46ca7b3fc6103c6","nasal":"d2bdc537253d1f1cd5e9bceba08307746f1c63715e1c767ef46ca7b3fc6103c6"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-19-24","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":19,"verse":24,"english":"There shall spring in the line of the highsouled Ikşvāku, one named Rāma son to Dasaratha who shall deprive your life.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":0.64,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-19-21"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7019024","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"76aeb32275116d43e21728dde7ba176ffb74112d84be0d5f2a96e4aaa01b892f","compact":"cbdcfdbbf0f4c920600d015d776c32532aeacbb42c3d563f1ef1980788db4a26","nasal":"85522f673f275c3c080b67a0c7ba57c62705e7c09c230d7fab7e74331b3ea8fc"}},{"id":"VRCE-7-19-25","kanda":7,"kandaId":"uttara","sarga":19,"verse":25,"english":"As he uttered this imprecation, the celestial kettle-drums sounded like the roaring of clouds; and blossoms showered down from the sky.","alignment":{"type":"1:1","confidence":1.0,"method":"shared-sanskrit-ngram","duttRefs":["DUTT-7-19-22"],"status":"unreviewed"},"source":{"sanskritLocator":"7019025","sanskritFile":"Ram07.txt","englishEdition":"M. N. Dutt 1891–94"},"sanskrit_fingerprints":{"exact":"cd272bcbfcbcf42eea7f8c1bcf4b886c0138e7958429d55dac81983d4afd4d49","compact":"c2857996790a5cb92239b7f4be3409a84783c103a0b31d99ba830b7ade9c4